0,Music of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_the_Andaman_and_Nicobar_Islands,"In 1888, the British naval officer Maurice Vidal Portman recorded Andamanese music and documented it using Western musical notation, which was published in the Journal of the Royal Asiatic Society. [3] Portman's writings stated that Andamanese songs only had timpani accompaniment. [3] Curt Sachs, the German musicologist, noted the culture of song-generation on the Andaman Islands among native ...","Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
1,Great Andamanese peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Andamanese_peoples,"The Great Andamanese are an indigenous people of the Great Andaman archipelago in the Andaman Islands. Historically, the Great Andamanese lived throughout the archipelago, and were divided into ten major tribes.","Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
2,Andamanese peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andamanese_peoples,"The Andamanese people included the Great Andamanese and Jarawas of the Great Andaman archipelago, the Onge of Little Andaman, and the Sentinelese of North Sentinel Island.[12] Among the Andamanese, a division of two groups can be made.","Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
3,Traditional Music of Andaman and Nicobar Islands - Thrillophilia,https://www.thrillophilia.com/blog/andaman-nicobar-traditional-music/,"Sep 29, 2025 · The traditional music of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands is a captivating blend of indigenous tribal rhythms and various multicultural influences. It highlights the diversity of music in songs, including Great Andamanese chants and Nicobari festival songs, providing examples of devotional and increasingly contemporary fusions, in presenting diversity as a point of celebration. The Duggera drum ...","Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
4,Mixed Great Andamanese | Endangered Languages Project,https://www.endangeredlanguages.com/elp-language/mixed-great-andamanese,"Abbi, Anvita. 2013. A Grammar of the Great Andamanese Language: An Ethnolinguistic Study. (Brill's Studies in South and Southwest Asian Languages.) Leiden: Brill. 330pp.","Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
5,Music of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Music_of_the_Andaman_and_Nicobar_Islands,"The music of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands encompasses a rich tapestry of indigenous tribal traditions and influences from settler communities, reflecting the archipelago's diverse ethnic groups including Negrito tribes like the Great Andamanese, Onge, Jarawa, and Sentinelese in the Andamans, as well as the Mongoloid Nicobarese and Shompen in ...","Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
6,Music of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands - Alchetron,https://alchetron.com/Music-of-the-Andaman-and-Nicobar-Islands,"Apr 25, 2026 · The main ethnic groups of the Andamans are the Andamanese, Onge, Jarawa, and Sentinalese. The main groups of Nicobar tribes are the Nicobari (Nicobarese) and Shompen. All these tribes have continued with their indigenous culture at Andaman and Nicobar islands, and still continue to do so.","Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
7,"Great Andamanese, Mixed | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/gac/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..Hd1g90yE6CzKNcnd1CtmsSfqOisrAspQsMU7Qg4g3ZI,Mixed Great Andamanese is a dormant language of India. It belongs to the Andamanese language family. The language is no longer used as a first language by any remaining members of the ethnic community.,"Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
8,"Great Andamanese, Mixed language. Evangelism tools, church...",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/gac,"Great Andamanese, Mixed language and dialect information. Audio Bible stories and lessons. Download free evangelism resources, MP3s, audio bible study tools, language/dialect information.","Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
9,Glottolog 5.1 - Mixed Great Andamanese,https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/mixe1288,"Great Andamanese, Mixed (gac-gac) = 9 (Dormant).But Mixed Great Andamanese cannot be asserted to be unintelligible with its source varieties, in particular Aka-Jeru [akj] ( Anvita Abbi 2013 ).","Great Andamanese, Mixed",Andamanese
